03:01:27,640 --> 03:01:28,460
Senator Joel Villanueva: Hindi naman po.

3379
03:01:29,100 --> 03:01:31,020
Senator Joel Villanueva: Getting from EBET, parang kulang.

3380
03:01:31,220 --> 03:01:39,200
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Ano po, nasa batas ho ninyo na pwede pong kumuha rin sa TWSP. So pwede pong TWSP at TTSP.

3381
03:01:39,200 --> 03:01:50,020
Senator Joel Villanueva: Exactly. That's why ako ang suggestion ko, I mean, at least look into it. Baka magandang ihiwalay-lagyan natin ang sariling item, yung EBET. Diba?

3382
03:01:50,020 --> 03:01:50,520
Senator Joel Villanueva: Pwede po.

3383
03:01:50,540 --> 03:01:52,260
Senator Joel Villanueva: Pwede po. Para mas ano na.

3384
03:01:52,280 --> 03:01:52,960
Senator Joel Villanueva: Pwede pwede po.

3385
03:01:53,040 --> 03:01:58,680
Senator Joel Villanueva: Mas klaro. And they just gave me an idea when I was listening to our Senate President. Yeah, please, please, please continue.

3386
03:02:01,580 --> 03:02:19,680
Senator Joel Villanueva: And Secretary, meron bang... Kasi merong... I think it's also the number of enterprises that join. So I remember talking to you about this na I think one of the parang concern or one of the complication,

3387
03:02:20,540 --> 03:02:31,160
Senator Joel Villanueva: there's a... At least dun sa na-experience ko, kailangan pa i-amend ng corporation ng kanilang Articles of Incorporation.

3388
03:02:31,880 --> 03:02:47,480
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, syempre sa kanila, parang hassle pa. Tapos, of course, kukuha ka pa ng abogado. So may mga ganun na maliliit na bagay. And also the claiming of incentives. I think this was also raised by EDCOM.

3389
03:02:47,480 --> 03:02:49,480
Senator Joel Villanueva: So may mga ganitong...

3390
03:02:50,540 --> 03:03:04,880
Senator Joel Villanueva: Overlook lang na agency na maliliit na bagay na sa atin maliit pero sa participating companies, hassle. Hassle sa kanila. Kaya huwag na lang. Huwag na tayo sumali dyan. So have you taken a look at this issue?

3391
03:03:04,880 --> 03:03:19,880
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Yes, sir. And in fact, it's not just the amendment of the Articles of Incorporation to include education and training as a provision. It's also things like TESDA guidelines, sir, required a...

3392
03:03:19,880 --> 03:03:35,140
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Ano talaga ba dyan? Notarized contract, sir, between the EBET provider or the enterprise and the learner. So we've tried to review all those guidelines in order to streamline them.

3393
03:03:35,140 --> 03:03:49,140
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We are hoping to comply with the EBET provisions on a digital one-stop shop by the fourth quarter, sir, of this year. So we're hoping that many of those little issues in terms of implementation...

3394
03:03:49,880 --> 03:04:07,760
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: can be overcome before we launch the digital one-stop shop. I am assuming that even after we do so, may lalabas pa rin po yan na mahirap na kailangan ding palitan ng TESDA in terms of its internal rules and guidelines.

3395
03:04:07,760 --> 03:04:18,760
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: But yes, sir, we understand that these are parts of the problem because the law, again, of Senator Joel...

3396
03:04:19,880 --> 03:04:40,380
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: It's TVI's from registering. So the enterprise has to take the lead in terms of its registration. And many of those enterprises actually are reluctant to create training plans and so on, would rather partner up as that kind of dual training system with an institution.

3397
03:04:40,380 --> 03:04:49,760
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: But the institution cannot, in fact, like they used to before the institution could register and partner up with an enterprise for the...

3398
03:04:49,880 --> 03:05:07,420
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: enterprise-based portion. Ngayon po, baliktad. And the TVI institution, the TECVOC institution cannot be the one to register, even if they are on behalf of the enterprise, right?

3399
03:05:07,420 --> 03:05:13,080
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Kung kahit na-partner sila, which is another one of those hurdles. But it is, sir, it's in the law.

3400
03:05:14,460 --> 03:05:16,740
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kung ngayon, yung enterprise, they need to partner.

3401
03:05:18,200 --> 03:05:19,480
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Not necessarily, sir.

3402
03:05:19,880 --> 03:05:23,860
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: But in many ways, that's probably the...

3403
03:05:23,860 --> 03:05:24,460
Senator Joel Villanueva: Most practical.

3404
03:05:24,460 --> 03:05:32,160
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Most practical for them to partner up with the TVI. But in fact, make the TVI help generate the training plan.

3405
03:05:34,000 --> 03:05:37,340
Senator Joel Villanueva: And they can actually be part of the assessment program, di ba?

3406
03:05:37,540 --> 03:05:38,060
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Yes, sir.

3407
03:05:38,320 --> 03:05:38,980
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yes, sir.

3408
03:05:39,080 --> 03:05:39,600
Senator Joel Villanueva: Enterprises.

3409
03:05:39,840 --> 03:05:40,260
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Yes, sir.

3410
03:05:41,320 --> 03:05:49,800
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: The last na lang siguro is one of the things that we've been looking forward to aside from the one-stop shop.

3411
03:05:50,040 --> 03:05:57,700
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: In fact, is to be able to finally fund the rollout of eBET integrators po, no?

3412
03:05:57,860 --> 03:06:00,200
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Kasi wala po sa budget namin.

3413
03:06:01,860 --> 03:06:13,560
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: EBET integrators po for small and micro enterprises that might not otherwise have the capacity to generate the training plans and so on needed, no?

3414
03:06:13,660 --> 03:06:15,740
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Or have the size and scale.

3415
03:06:17,620 --> 03:06:18,800
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Nasa batas nyo rin po yan.

3416
03:06:18,800 --> 03:06:19,720
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yes, I was just...

3417
03:06:19,720 --> 03:06:24,660
Senator Joel Villanueva: Just given the, you know, yung three points that still pending, no?

3418
03:06:24,720 --> 03:06:32,680
Senator Joel Villanueva: Itong eBET support integrators, itong eBET one-stop shop, and itong eBET grievance mechanism still pending.

3419
03:06:33,720 --> 03:06:40,140
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Ang eBET grievance mechanism, sir, internal to the enterprises, we require them to have one.

3420
03:06:40,660 --> 03:06:42,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: There's no guidelines pa, e.

3421
03:06:42,700 --> 03:06:43,000
Senator Joel Villanueva: Di ba?

3422
03:06:43,560 --> 03:06:48,000
Senator Joel Villanueva: Wala pa yung guidelines on mechanism on addressing disputes.

3423
03:06:48,000 --> 03:06:50,820
Senator Joel Villanueva: Disputes on eBET implementations?

3424
03:06:50,960 --> 03:06:51,340
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Yes, sir.

3425
03:06:51,660 --> 03:06:55,580
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So, we will come up with that also like in the next two weeks.

3426
03:06:55,860 --> 03:06:56,300
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Tama ba?

3427
03:06:56,860 --> 03:06:58,940
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: It's going through the process.

3428
03:06:59,580 --> 03:06:59,840
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sige.

3429
03:07:00,160 --> 03:07:01,080
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sorry, SP.

3430
03:07:01,260 --> 03:07:01,940
Senator Joel Villanueva: Please continue.

3431
03:07:02,780 --> 03:07:06,460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Bottom line lang, Secretary, is just take a look at the...

3432
03:07:06,460 --> 03:07:08,780
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Those mga maliliit na bagay lang, no?

3433
03:07:09,000 --> 03:07:11,900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: These are things that we might have overlooked.

3434
03:07:12,900 --> 03:07:17,840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pero nakaka-ano siya, nakaka-discouraged ng participants, no?

3435
03:07:17,840 --> 03:07:18,880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Especially for eBET.

3436
03:07:19,420 --> 03:07:24,620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But this, in eBET is particularly, lahat naman tayo sinusuportahan ito, no?

3437
03:07:24,620 --> 03:07:25,900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because we all know the outcome.

3438
03:07:26,540 --> 03:07:29,400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, maraming salamat, Mr. Chairman.

3439
03:07:29,520 --> 03:07:31,180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you for the opportunity.

3440
03:07:31,520 --> 03:07:36,060
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Mr. Chairman, I keep on saying your law, pero principal authors...

3441
03:07:36,060 --> 03:07:44,840
Senator Joel Villanueva: Without your support and without the staff support of EDGOM, we would not be able to...

3442
03:07:44,840 --> 03:07:47,740
Senator Joel Villanueva: We'll never be able to finish.

3443
03:07:47,840 --> 03:07:51,380
Senator Joel Villanueva: This particular bill that became a law.

3444
03:07:51,380 --> 03:08:02,400
Senator Joel Villanueva: Anyway, thank you so much to our Senate President who is also a candidate for being Secretary of TESDA

3445
03:08:02,400 --> 03:08:11,980
Senator Joel Villanueva: because he knows very well how TESDA works, how everything works from the little things

3446
03:08:11,980 --> 03:08:16,180
Senator Joel Villanueva: and all these scholarship programs na very confusing sometimes.

3447
03:08:17,020 --> 03:08:17,380
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you.

3448
03:08:17,380 --> 03:08:17,820
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you.

3449
03:08:17,820 --> 03:08:21,720
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you very much again and we appreciate the presence of our Senate President.

3450
03:08:22,180 --> 03:08:23,980
Senator Joel Villanueva: Just a few more questions, no?

3451
03:08:24,440 --> 03:08:31,300
Senator Joel Villanueva: Let me go to another topic that is very dear to me, itong lifelong learning.

3452
03:08:32,000 --> 03:08:40,100
Senator Joel Villanueva: Given that TESDA has a central role in TVET and skills development under this particular law

3453
03:08:40,100 --> 03:08:47,660
Senator Joel Villanueva: that we all supported, by the way, and as part of EDCOM, we are all espousing itong Lifelong Learning

3454
03:08:47,800 --> 03:08:49,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: Development Framework Act.

3455
03:08:49,860 --> 03:09:00,480
Senator Joel Villanueva: May we know, in this year's budget, how much was programmed or identified for the initial implementation?

3456
03:09:00,700 --> 03:09:11,920
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kasi ano yan eh, as of August 31, diba, part of the law, yung section 14, provides that initial implementation

3457
03:09:11,920 --> 03:09:15,620
Senator Joel Villanueva: shall be funded from the existing budgets of the concerned agencies, no?

3458
03:09:15,620 --> 03:09:17,620
Senator Joel Villanueva: And then for 2026, magkakaka...

3459
03:09:17,800 --> 03:09:23,180
Senator Joel Villanueva: Paano yung akikita natin na magiging part niyan?

3460
03:09:23,760 --> 03:09:27,360
Senator Joel Villanueva: 2026, anyway, merong na-obligate dito, no?

3461
03:09:28,260 --> 03:09:29,920
Senator Joel Villanueva: In the disperse? Wala.

3462
03:09:30,280 --> 03:09:32,260
Senator Joel Villanueva: For lifelong learning.

3463
03:09:32,260 --> 03:09:39,380
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Ang ginawa namin, sa totoo lang, as you know, kalalabas lang po ng IRR

3464
03:09:39,380 --> 03:09:45,860
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: at hindi pa po lumalabas ang master plan ng PQF National Coordinating Council.

3465
03:09:45,860 --> 03:09:51,400
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And in the absence of that, in terms of targeting lifelong learning efforts per se,

3466
03:09:51,400 --> 03:10:04,680
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: what we have been doing has been using our current budgets for things like creative industries, right?

3467
03:10:04,760 --> 03:10:12,560
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: For things that may not look like they are directly related to employment per se,

3468
03:10:13,080 --> 03:10:15,740
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: but might be for culture, for heritage.

3469
03:10:15,860 --> 03:10:17,680
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So on and so forth.

3470
03:10:18,180 --> 03:10:23,140
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: All of that, sir, is going to be part of the lifelong learning rollout, particularly for LGUs,

3471
03:10:23,240 --> 03:10:30,580
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: which is also, after all, part of the proposal to get DILG to spearhead its implementation.

3472
03:10:31,280 --> 03:10:35,300
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So sa ngayon, sir, yun pa lang ang aming mga nilalagay or ginagawa.

3473
03:10:35,820 --> 03:10:40,880
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Wala pa pong identified line item that says this is lifelong learning.

3474
03:10:40,880 --> 03:10:45,680
Senator Joel Villanueva: I was about to say that.

3475
03:10:45,860 --> 03:10:54,720
Senator Joel Villanueva: I'm happy to note that the Secretary of TESDA is now the chairperson of the PQF National Referencing Committee.

3476
03:10:55,260 --> 03:10:59,780
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Sir, referencing committee po kami, hindi po kami sa lifelong learning.

3477
03:10:59,980 --> 03:11:05,680
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yeah, but considering that you are there, nasa kanila yung bola, at least maano natin yan.

3478
03:11:05,680 --> 03:11:15,740
Senator Joel Villanueva: And of course, that brings me to my next point, how much allocated for 2026 and for 2027.

3479
03:11:15,860 --> 03:11:25,740
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kasi laki nung responsibility na binibigay sa TESDA's work under the Philippine Qualifications Framework

3480
03:11:25,740 --> 03:11:28,460
Senator Joel Villanueva: and the National Referencing Committee.

3481
03:11:29,420 --> 03:11:34,180
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Sir, ang budget po niyan nasa DepEd. Wala po sa TESDA.

3482
03:11:35,460 --> 03:11:36,320
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ano? Allocation?

3483
03:11:36,600 --> 03:11:40,500
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Wala po. Walang specific po for the PQF work.

3484
03:11:40,500 --> 03:11:45,100
Senator Joel Villanueva: What's your view on that?

3485
03:11:45,100 --> 03:11:45,700
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: At the moment?

3486
03:11:45,860 --> 03:11:47,660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Sir, there is still actually…

3487
03:11:47,660 --> 03:11:48,960
Senator Joel Villanueva: We can get a line item for that?

3488
03:11:49,200 --> 03:11:53,280
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Pwede naman, sir. Kaya lang. Sa totoo lang, may unused pa po sa DepEd eh.

3489
03:11:53,780 --> 03:11:57,200
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: The budget is actually at DepEd and they haven't actually used it yet.

3490
03:11:58,220 --> 03:11:59,880
Senator Joel Villanueva: So ililipat na lang namin, sir.

3491
03:11:59,900 --> 03:12:02,240
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Pero sila po ang chair ng PQF Council.

3492
03:12:02,240 --> 03:12:04,480
Senator Joel Villanueva: I know, I know. I'm just kidding.

3493
03:12:04,960 --> 03:12:11,560
Senator Joel Villanueva: At saka si Senator Angare is more than capable of bringing reforms.

3494
03:12:13,000 --> 03:12:15,240
Senator Joel Villanueva: Anyway, when we test the complete…

3495
03:12:15,240 --> 03:12:26,820
Senator Joel Villanueva: We can submit itong Philippines Updated AQRF, yung re-referencing report to the ASEAN Qualifications Referencing Framework Committee.

3496
03:12:26,820 --> 03:12:34,900
Senator Joel Villanueva: And perhaps the next question would be what remaining steps must be completed before the endorsement and the publication ito?

3497
03:12:35,200 --> 03:12:38,740
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Sir, it's ongoing and there is in fact…

3498
03:12:38,740 --> 03:12:40,320
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Actually, Rose, ikaw kaya sumagot.

3499
03:12:40,720 --> 03:12:43,240
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ikaw kaya mag-attend sa meeting.

3500
03:12:44,040 --> 03:12:45,080
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ikaw nga ang sumagot.

3501
03:12:47,700 --> 03:12:51,260
Senator Joel Villanueva: Namimiss ka na rin, namimiss na rin ni SPWin yung boses mo.

3502
03:12:53,320 --> 03:13:00,660
TESDA Deputy Director General Rosanna Urdaneta: The last AQRF was held in Bangkok, Thailand a month ago.

3503
03:13:01,260 --> 03:13:09,440
TESDA Deputy Director General Rosanna Urdaneta: And we have promised that we have committed that we shall submit the updated report on December.

3504
03:13:10,160 --> 03:13:11,220
TESDA Deputy Director General Rosanna Urdaneta: of this year.

3505
03:13:11,280 --> 03:13:11,820
Senator Joel Villanueva: This year.

3506
03:13:11,820 --> 03:13:12,080
Senator Joel Villanueva: Okay.

3507
03:13:12,080 --> 03:13:14,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: Okay.

3508
03:13:15,220 --> 03:13:15,740
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sige.

3509
03:13:16,280 --> 03:13:18,100
Senator Joel Villanueva: We'll look forward to it.

3510
03:13:18,540 --> 03:13:19,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you.

3511
03:13:19,240 --> 03:13:22,100
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Sorry, Mr. Chair, if I may line just to be even more specific.

3512
03:13:23,060 --> 03:13:38,080
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: The request of the ASEAN Qualifications Referencing Framework has been for us to do an update of our report rather than to re-reference because of the number of reforms, no?

3513
03:13:38,080 --> 03:13:41,080
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: That we have undertaken that was not part of the original…

3514
03:13:42,080 --> 03:13:43,080
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Re-referencing.

3515
03:13:43,080 --> 03:13:54,680
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So, at this point, what the committee is doing is, in fact, updating the original referencing report to include the new level descriptors and so on and so forth.

3516
03:13:54,680 --> 03:13:58,700
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And the timeline is supposed to be by December this year.

3517
03:13:59,720 --> 03:14:00,420
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you.

3518
03:14:00,680 --> 03:14:01,780
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you very much.

3519
03:14:01,780 --> 03:14:11,740
Senator Joel Villanueva: Unless our Senate President or anyone would like to, perhaps, I don't want to preempt the Senate President's motion.

3520
03:14:12,080 --> 03:14:19,980
Senator Joel Villanueva: To deem the, I mean, to submit for plenary consideration the…

3521
03:14:19,980 --> 03:14:27,400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, it's a pleasure to submit the budget of TESDA to plenary for further discussions and approval.

3522
03:14:28,140 --> 03:14:35,560
Senator Joel Villanueva: There is a motion rendered no other than the Senate President of the Republic of the Philippines.

3523
03:14:36,220 --> 03:14:38,060
Senator Joel Villanueva: How can we object to that?

3524
03:14:38,400 --> 03:14:40,840
Senator Joel Villanueva: And hearing no objection, the motion is carried.

3525
03:14:41,480 --> 03:14:41,600
Senator Joel Villanueva: And so…

3526
03:14:42,080 --> 03:14:57,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, we, the fiscal year 2027 proposed budget of the TESDA is now hereby submitted for plenary consideration subject to the discussions and submission of requested documents by our colleagues.

3527
03:14:57,320 --> 03:14:59,720
Senator Joel Villanueva: Maraming salamat po to everyone.

3528
03:15:00,000 --> 03:15:12,460
Senator Joel Villanueva: Again, I'd like to take this opportunity to thank our Senate President, the hardworking Senate President who keeps on pushing us to work in the wee hours of the morning.

3529
03:15:13,980 --> 03:15:26,300
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I think most of my time spent here in the Senate, I think at least 70% of my day spent here in the Senate or 80% of my day.

3530
03:15:26,380 --> 03:15:29,100
Senator Joel Villanueva: But we're happy to work with our Senate President.

3531
03:15:29,100 --> 03:15:47,540
Senator Joel Villanueva: Of course, thank you, Secretary Kiko Benitez, DDG Galo, DDG Urdaneta, DDG Vidal, DDG Allan, and Directors, Provincial Directors, Regional Directors, Executive Directors, of course, our friends from COA.

3532
03:15:47,720 --> 03:15:49,340
Senator Joel Villanueva: Maraming salamat po sa inyong lahat.

3533
03:15:49,860 --> 03:15:55,620
Senator Joel Villanueva: This budget briefing is hereby suspended. Maraming salamat po sa inyo and may God bless us all. Salamat po.

